WEBVTT

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.859
Welcome to Homlle safe visits awareness.

00:00:03.079 --> 00:00:04.992
Your role is to provide the

00:00:04.992 --> 00:00:06.586
agreed cleaning or beauty service.

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:10.037
You are not a carer, babysitter or investigator.

00:00:10.257 --> 00:00:13.010
Before working alone, know the named duty

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:15.371
contact, check-in plan and emergency route.

00:00:15.591 --> 00:00:18.833
These arrangements must actually be staffed and tested.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:23.125
Before the visit, check the address, access and known risks.

00:00:23.345 --> 00:00:25.909
Have a charged phone and an agreed check-in

00:00:25.909 --> 00:00:28.474
and check-out plan with someone who can respond.

00:00:28.694 --> 00:00:32.107
An app notification is not an emergency service.

00:00:32.327 --> 00:00:34.822
If the situation changes or you feel

00:00:34.822 --> 00:00:37.318
threatened, leave when safe and contact help.

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:41.221
Before a lone visit, agree who will respond, when contact

00:00:41.221 --> 00:00:44.049
is expected and what happens if you miss it.

00:00:44.269 --> 00:00:46.589
A phone notification that nobody monitors

00:00:46.589 --> 00:00:48.523
is not a safety system.

00:00:48.743 --> 00:00:52.389
Test the contact route without calling emergency services.

00:00:52.609 --> 00:00:55.573
If the phone fails or the risk is beyond the

00:00:55.573 --> 00:00:58.241
agreed limits, move to safety and pause the visit.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:01.291
If you encounter threats, aggression or conditions

00:01:01.291 --> 00:01:03.503
outside the safe plan, do not argue

00:01:03.503 --> 00:01:05.714
or try to prove you can cope.

00:01:05.934 --> 00:01:08.536
Leave safely where possible and seek help.

00:01:08.756 --> 00:01:12.199
Serious immediate danger needs emergency services.

00:01:12.419 --> 00:01:14.753
Tell the duty contact once safe.

00:01:14.973 --> 00:01:17.555
Homlle must set clear limits on what lone

00:01:17.555 --> 00:01:19.814
workers can do and arrange suitable support.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.192
Cleaning can create hazards for other people.

00:01:23.412 --> 00:01:26.344
Keep people away from wet slippery floors using

00:01:26.344 --> 00:01:28.909
suitable barriers or working in sections; a

00:01:28.909 --> 00:01:31.474
warning sign alone does not prevent access.

00:01:31.694 --> 00:01:34.637
Keep the exit clear and manage trailing cables.

00:01:34.857 --> 00:01:37.117
Only reopen the area when safe.

00:01:37.337 --> 00:01:39.539
Ask for help if you cannot separate

00:01:39.539 --> 00:01:41.741
the work from customers, children or pets.

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:44.734
You may notice a person being

00:01:44.734 --> 00:01:46.887
threatened, neglected or pressured for money.

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:49.899
Listen calmly and record relevant facts,

00:01:49.899 --> 00:01:52.225
keeping observation separate from opinion.

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:55.399
Do not question people like an investigator,

00:01:55.399 --> 00:01:58.353
confront a suspected abuser or promise secrecy.

00:01:58.573 --> 00:02:00.582
Explain that you may need to share

00:02:00.582 --> 00:02:02.304
information with people who can help.

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:05.768
If someone is in immediate danger or an

00:02:05.768 --> 00:02:08.119
emergency crime is happening, call nine nine

00:02:08.119 --> 00:02:10.471
nine and move to safety if possible.

00:02:10.691 --> 00:02:13.335
Do not wait for a routine manager reply.

00:02:13.555 --> 00:02:15.796
Do not attempt an unsafe rescue.

00:02:16.016 --> 00:02:19.154
Once safe, report through the agreed Homlle route

00:02:19.154 --> 00:02:21.901
so further protective action can be coordinated.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:25.837
For a non-immediate concern, contact the safeguarding lead

00:02:25.837 --> 00:02:28.600
or deputy promptly and follow the appropriate

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:31.362
local authority or police route when needed.

00:02:31.582 --> 00:02:35.297
Record times, observations, relevant words and actions.

00:02:35.517 --> 00:02:39.025
Use a secure channel and share only what is necessary.

00:02:39.245 --> 00:02:41.063
Do not post the situation in

00:02:41.063 --> 00:02:42.881
a group chat or public review.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.753
A customer says someone is threatening them

00:02:45.753 --> 00:02:47.529
and asks you to tell nobody.

00:02:47.749 --> 00:02:49.606
Do not promise secrecy.

00:02:49.826 --> 00:02:52.993
Listen, explain that help may require sharing

00:02:52.993 --> 00:02:55.708
relevant information, and assess immediate danger.

00:02:55.928 --> 00:02:59.149
Follow the safeguarding route and record facts securely.

00:02:59.369 --> 00:03:01.683
Your job is to raise the concern,

00:03:01.683 --> 00:03:03.666
not decide the whole case yourself.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:06.970
Complete the knowledge check and rehearse how to

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:09.460
contact help and respond to a missed check-in.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:12.047
A supervisor must confirm that the

00:03:12.047 --> 00:03:14.414
contact details and escalation plan work.

00:03:14.634 --> 00:03:16.799
Record the lesson and assessment.

00:03:17.019 --> 00:03:20.421
This awareness lesson does not replace a safeguarding

00:03:20.421 --> 00:03:23.823
lead, local procedures or a trained emergency response.

00:03:24.043 --> 00:03:26.863
Your assessor should check understanding, correct any

00:03:26.863 --> 00:03:29.684
gaps and observe the relevant practical skills.

00:03:29.904 --> 00:03:33.699
Do not treat video completion as automatic permission to work.
